  "notes": "Nice One Beauty Digital Marketing Company (ticker 4193, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/6866_0_2026-03-31...). Auditor: Ernst & Young Professional Services; unqualified opinion. The consolidated financial statements were approved and authorized to issue by the Board of Directors on 27 Ramadan 1447H (corresponding to 16 March 2026) - Note 32. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1) except per-share data. The primary statements (printed FS pages 6-9) are scanned images (DocuSigned) in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.7x); the notes are digital text. Consolidated group; there is **NO non-controlling interest** (net profit and equity are not split), so only total_equity is carried. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. **FY2025 was Nice One's first full year as a listed company** - the December 2024 IPO proceeds (SAR 5.5m to share capital + SAR 185.2m to share premium, cash-flow line 'Issuance of share capital' + 'share premium portion' = SAR 192.5m, carried as capital_increase_proceeds) were used to repay all borrowings, so the Group is now debt-free (long_term_debt / current_debt were carried for FY2024 only). additional_paid_in_capital is 'Share premium' (nil FY2024); other_reserves is the 'Statutory reserve' (SAR 318,900 at end-2024, not yet re-appropriated at end-2025). related_party_receivables is 'Amounts due from related parties' (nil FY2025); accounts_payable is 'Trade payables, accruals and other payables'; lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the reported lease-liability portions; defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employees' defined benefit liabilities'; zakat_payable is 'Zakat provision'. On the P&L: operating_income is 'OPERATING PROFIT'; finance_costs / finance_income are the reported lines (finance income nil FY2024); other_income is 'Other (expenses) income, net' (a small net expense in FY2025, a small net income in FY2024); income_taxes_and_zakat is 'Zakat'. **FY2025 effective zakat is 66.6% of the (collapsed) pre-tax profit - zakat is levied on the zakat base / equity, not on income - so the effective-tax plausibility bound warns (expected).** On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E depreciation, right-of-use-asset depreciation and intangible-asset amortisation; interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; capex combines 'Purchase of property and equipment' and 'Purchase of intangible assets'; debt_repaid combines 'Repayments of long-term borrowings' and 'Repayments of short-term borrowings'; debt_issued is 'Proceeds from short-term borrowings' (FY2024 only); lease_payments is 'Repayment of principal of lease liabilities'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid' (FY2024 only); capital_increase_proceeds is the FY2025 IPO cash inflow; the cash-flow statement has no FX-on-cash line and its closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. **Rough year** - a large step-up in selling/marketing and G&A spend (SAR 146.2m -> 178.9m and SAR 42.9m -> 55.8m) took operating profit from SAR 79.0m to SAR 10.3m and net profit from SAR 71.7m to SAR 3.0m, EPS 0.03 (FY2024 0.65). Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 6, comprehensive income 7, changes in equity 8, cash flows 9.",
